{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_12_constitution_article_xxiii", "label": "Article XXIII \u2014 No conclusion is immune from re-examination", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-30-section-text.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_10_agent_handoff_invariant_2", "label": "Invariant 2 \u2014 Projections are written only by Ledger::Apply", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-30-section-text.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "implementation_implemented_stage_30_section_text_stage", "label": "Stage 30 \u2014 The whole text, readable in Galedra (implemented)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-30-section-text.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A person reading an outline should be able to read the source: a leaf holds the text of its own passage, a branch composes its leaves, the root shows the whole transcript. The Moonshots outline had 35 anchors totalling 4,514 characters standing in for a multi-hour episode, and the page labelled an anchor \"the passage this section covers\", which is the misreading that prompted the stage."}, {"id": "implementation_implemented_stage_30_section_text_anchor_reading_split", "label": "Anchor versus reading \u2014 a cleaned transcript is not a quotation", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-30-section-text.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The two must never be the same field. An anchor is the leaf's opening words verbatim, hashed and checked against the fetched source; a reading is the full text cleaned by an assistant, hashed over the cleaned text and never checked, displayed as an attributed, dated transcription. The moment an assistant fixes transcription errors, what it produces is a model's reading of the source, and model output is never evidence by itself. Collapsing the distinction would make Galedra a place where edited speech is attributed to real people with a hash beside it."}, {"id": "implementation_implemented_stage_30_section_text_branches_compose", "label": "A branch composes its leaves, it does not store text", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-30-section-text.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Sections::Text walks the subtree in document order and assembles readings at read time, so there is exactly one copy of anything, a correction to one leaf corrects every level above it, and the composition stays derived (Invariant 2). The root's page is the whole transcript without a transcript ever being written twice."}, {"id": "implementation_implemented_stage_30_section_text_cleaning_rule", "label": "The narrow cleaning rule (a speaker who misspeaks stays misspoken)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-30-section-text.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "\"Fix errors\" is an invitation to rewrite, so the rule is deliberately narrow and negative: paragraphs where the speaker changes subject, misheard words, mangled proper nouns and punctuation, [unclear] for what cannot be made out, and nothing else. No tidying grammar, no removing repetition or filler, no summarising, no reordering, and no reconstructing from memory \u2014 the misspeaking is often the thing worth checking."}, {"id": "implementation_implemented_stage_30_section_text_retrieval_excludes_by_id", "label": "Retrieval excludes readings by identity, not by locator type", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-30-section-text.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The obvious filter \u2014 stop checking TRANSCRIPTION locations \u2014 would break Stage 13's legitimate use, text an assistant read off an image, which should still be looked for. So the exclusion is by id, from the set of locations that are some section's reading. Reporting a reading as not found would report a failure that is not one, because it never was a quotation."}], "edges": [{"source": "implementation_implemented_stage_30_section_text_stage", "target": "implementation_implemented_stage_30_section_text_anchor_reading_split", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-30-section-text.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "implementation_implemented_stage_30_section_text_stage", "target": "implementation_implemented_stage_30_section_text_branches_compose", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-30-section-text.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "implementation_implemented_stage_30_section_text_stage", "target": "implementation_implemented_stage_30_section_text_cleaning_rule", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-30-section-text.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "implementation_implemented_stage_30_section_text_stage", "target": "implementation_implemented_stage_30_section_text_retrieval_excludes_by_id", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-30-section-text.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "implementation_implemented_stage_30_section_text_branches_compose", "target": "app_services_sections_text_text", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-30-section-text.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "implementation_implemented_stage_30_section_text_anchor_reading_split", "target": "app_services_ledger_apply_apply", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-30-section-text.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "implementation_implemented_stage_30_section_text_anchor_reading_split", "target": "app_models_section_section", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-30-section-text.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "implementation_implemented_stage_30_section_text_retrieval_excludes_by_id", "target": "app_services_sources_retrieve_retrieve", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-30-section-text.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "implementation_implemented_stage_30_section_text_retrieval_excludes_by_id", "target": "implementation_implemented_stage_17_retrieval_stage", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-30-section-text.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "implementation_implemented_stage_30_section_text_stage", "target": "implementation_implemented_stage_20_sections_create_section", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-30-section-text.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "implementation_i